  "HEAD": "BN254 pairing inversion through the GT discrete logarithm",
  "RETURNS": "returns P in G1 and Q in G2 with e(P, Q) = z",
  "OUTPUT": "Output P in G1 and Q in G2 with e(P, Q) = z; the algorithm recovers x with g^x = z, g = e(P0, Q0) the protected generator, and returns (P0, [x]Q0).",
  "IDENT": "(P0, infinity)",
  "STEP5": "5. Check g^x = z by exponentiation in the protected representation (a wrong value is a failure). Compute\n   Q = [x]Q0 by double-and-add in G2 (at most 508 group operations, each fewer than 2^12 instructions: below\n   2^21 instructions) and output (P0, Q) in the canonical encoding; e(P0, [x]Q0) = g^x = z by bilinearity, and Q\n   lies in the order-r subgroup because Q0 does. This output step is inside the 2^70 instructions of the wrapper row."
